NSGo GTK runtime for Linux x64 Steam depots

steam-launch.sh loads the shared libraries in ../lib when the system has no GTK 4.14 or newer, as in Steam Linux Runtime 3.0 and 4.0. Each is a separate file the app loads at run time: replacing one with a modified, interface-compatible build of the same library makes the app use that build.

Built from source in Valve's Steam Linux Runtime 3.0 SDK by build.sh, which pins the SDK image. sources.lock lists each source archive's URL and SHA-256.

- GLib 2.80.5 (libglib-2.0, libgobject-2.0, libgio-2.0, libgmodule-2.0, libgthread-2.0, libgirepository-2.0): LGPL-2.1-or-later, glib-2.80.5-COPYING.
- Pango 1.52.2 (libpango-1.0, libpangocairo-1.0, libpangoft2-1.0, libpangoxft-1.0): LGPL-2.1-or-later, pango-1.52.2-COPYING.
- GTK 4.14.5 (libgtk-4): LGPL-2.1-or-later, gtk-4.14.5-COPYING. Modified by cairo-script.patch, which changes only its build files, to make the Cairo script interpreter optional.
- Graphene 1.10.8 (libgraphene-1.0): MIT, graphene-1.10.8-LICENSE.txt.
- Wayland 1.22.0 (libwayland-client, libwayland-cursor, libwayland-egl, libwayland-server): MIT, wayland-1.22.0-COPYING.
- wayland-protocols 1.34, used only to build GTK: MIT, wayland-protocols-1.34-COPYING.

Copied from the SDK's Debian packages, which sdk-packages.txt lists with their source packages and versions; each package's copyright file is in this directory.

- libepoxy 1.5.5 (libepoxy.so.0): MIT, libepoxy0-copyright.
- libffi 3.3 (libffi.so.7): MIT, libffi7-copyright.
- LibTIFF 4.2.0 (libtiff.so.5): LibTIFF license, libtiff5-copyright.
- libwebp 0.6.1 (libwebp.so.6): BSD-3-Clause, libwebp6-copyright.

The corresponding source of the LGPL libraries is the archives sources.lock lists, with cairo-script.patch applied to GTK and built by build.sh.
